      "why": "Clockwise, counter-clockwise and alternating spinners sit in one cluster, so one block leaving turns its neighbours different ways, and the order of escapes decides where each one ends up pointing. Three Sequence blocks can only take their first step when their first lane is clear, which ties them to the cluster: the red one at R1C3 points down column 3 and must wait until the cluster has emptied that column, then comes back pointing left. The two spinners that can leave at once (G at R4C3 down, P at R3C1 left) are both wrong at the start: each turns two neighbours of different rules too early, and the failure shows up to 11 moves later. Limitation: no spinner touches a Sequence block, so the Sequence advances turn nothing here; Sequence works through its lane condition only.",
