      "why": "Three magnets and six spinners. A magnet that leaves drags the first block behind it into the cell it left, so lanes are created and destroyed, and here the solution is a chain. Every winning line uses the same three pulls in the same order (checked exhaustively). Move 1: the yellow magnet at R5C1 leaves down and drags the blue spinner at R4C1 into its place. Later the green magnet at R1C5 leaves right and drags the purple magnet from R1C1 along the whole top row into R1C5 - only possible once G at R1C2 has left down. The purple magnet then leaves up and drags Y at R4C5 up column 5 into the empty top row, from where it leaves left. Each magnet pulls whatever is first behind it at that moment, so the player has to plan the order before pulling. Only 1 of the 4 legal first moves keeps the board solvable. Without magnets the board cannot be solved at all.",
